<header class="ref-head yr-head"><p class="cty-kicker">Year by year · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p><h1 class="research-title">1940</h1><p class="ref-lede">1940 in world history: 41 events, 16 births, 20 deaths, 1 work, 8 states founded and 5 that came to an end. 711 recorded states existed that year.</p></header>
<nav class="ref-letters yr-near" aria-label="Nearby years"><a href="/years/1936">1936</a><a href="/years/1937">1937</a><a href="/years/1938">1938</a><a href="/years/1939">1939</a><a href="/years/1940" aria-current="page">1940</a><a href="/years/1941">1941</a><a href="/years/1942">1942</a><a href="/years/1943">1943</a><a href="/years/1944">1944</a></nav>
<section><h2 class="ref-sec-title">Events</h2><ol class="day-events yr-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/january-8">8 January</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Britain introduces food rationing</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Bacon, butter and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sugar-plantation">sugar</a> became the first foods rationed in wartime <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a>. Rationing extended to most foods during the war and did not end entirely until 1954.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/january-31">31 January</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">First monthly Social Security cheque is issued</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Ida May Fuller, a retired legal secretary from Vermont, received cheque number 00-000-001 for 22.54 dollars. She lived to 100 and collected about 22,000 dollars in benefits.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/february-10">10 February</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Soviet Union begins mass deportations from eastern Poland</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nkvd">NKVD</a> deported some 140,000 Polish citizens, many of them families of settlers and foresters, to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/siberia">Siberia</a> and Kazakhstan. It was the first of four <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/deportation">mass deportations</a> in 1940-41.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soviet-union">Soviet Union</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/siberia">Siberia</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/march-13">13 March</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Winter War ends as the Moscow Peace Treaty takes effect</h3><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/finland">Finland</a> ceded about a tenth of its territory, including <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/karelia">Karelia</a>, to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soviet-union">Soviet Union</a>. Its stubborn defence had cost the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/red-army">Red Army</a> heavily and preserved Finnish independence.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soviet-union">Soviet Union</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/finland">Finland</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/karelia">Karelia</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/north-sea" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/north-sea.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/april-9">9 April</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Germany invades Denmark and Norway</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">German forces struck both neutral states in Operation Weserübung. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/denmark">Denmark</a> yielded within hours, while <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/norway">Norway</a>, aided by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>, fought on for two months, giving <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a> vital <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-sea">North Sea</a> and Atlantic bases.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-sea">North Sea</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/denmark">Denmark</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/norway">Norway</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/may-10">10 May</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Churchill becomes Prime Minister as Germany attacks in the West</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">As German forces invaded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-the-netherlands">Netherlands</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/belgium">Belgium</a> and Luxembourg, Neville Chamberlain resigned and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/winston-churchill">Winston Churchill</a> formed a coalition government to lead <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a>'s war.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/belgium">Belgium</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/may-13">13 May</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Churchill offers 'blood, toil, tears and sweat'</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">In his first speech to the Commons as Prime Minister, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/winston-churchill">Winston Churchill</a> promised a long struggle and declared his aim to be 'victory at all costs'.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/may-15">15 May</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Nylon stockings go on sale across the United States</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Shoppers bought some four million pairs of DuPont nylon stockings on the first day of nationwide sales. The synthetic fibre transformed fashion and was soon diverted to wartime parachutes.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/may-20">20 May</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">First prisoners are brought to Auschwitz</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Thirty German criminal prisoners arrived from Sachsenhausen to act as camp functionaries. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oswiecim">Auschwitz</a> grew into the largest Nazi death camp, where about 1.1 million people, most of them <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jews">Jews</a>, were murdered.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/may-26">26 May</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Evacuation of Allied troops from Dunkirk begins</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Operation Dynamo began. By 4 June more than 338,000 British and French soldiers had been carried to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a> by warships and hundreds of civilian 'little ships'.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/may-28">28 May</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">King Leopold III surrenders the Belgian army</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">After eighteen days of fighting, Leopold III capitulated to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a> against his government's wishes. The surrender exposed the Allied flank as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dunkirk">Dunkirk</a> evacuation gathered pace.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/paris" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/paris.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/june-3">3 June</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Luftwaffe bombs Paris</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">In Operation Paula, German aircraft struck airfields and factories around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a>, killing some 250 people. Eleven days later German troops entered the city.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/june-4">4 June</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Churchill vows 'we shall fight on the beaches'</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">As the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dunkirk">Dunkirk</a> evacuation ended, Churchill told the Commons it was not a victory but promised that <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> would 'never surrender'.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/paris" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/paris.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/june-14">14 June</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">German troops enter Paris</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wehrmacht">Wehrmacht</a> marched into the French capital, which had been declared an open city. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> signed an <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/armistice-of-11-november-1918">armistice</a> eight days later.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/charles-de-gaulle" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/charles-de-gaulle.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/june-18">18 June</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">De Gaulle calls on the French to fight on</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Speaking on the BBC from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a>, General <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-de-gaulle">Charles de Gaulle</a> rejected the coming <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/armistice-of-11-november-1918">armistice</a> and urged French forces to continue resistance. The appeal founded the Free French movement.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/french-empire">French Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-de-gaulle">Charles de Gaulle</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/july-10">10 July</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">The Battle of Britain begins</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/luftwaffe">Luftwaffe</a> began attacking Channel convoys and coastal targets, the date <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> uses for the start of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-britain">Battle of Britain</a>. The RAF's survival over four months forced Hitler to postpone his invasion.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/mexico-city" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mexico-city.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/august-20">20 August</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Leon Trotsky is struck with an ice axe in Mexico City</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Soviet agent Ramón Mercader attacked <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/leon-trotsky">Leon Trotsky</a> in his study in Coyoacán; Trotsky died the next day. Stalin had pursued his exiled rival for over a decade.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexico-city">Mexico City</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/london" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/london.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/september-7">7 September</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">The Blitz begins with a massive raid on London</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/luftwaffe">Luftwaffe</a> switched to bombing <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a>, starting 57 consecutive nights of raids. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/the-blitz">The Blitz</a> killed some 43,000 civilians by May 1941 but failed to break British morale.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/london" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/london.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/september-15">15 September</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">The RAF repels massed daylight raids on Battle of Britain Day</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/luftwaffe">Luftwaffe</a> launched two huge raids on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a> and lost around 60 aircraft. Two days later Hitler postponed his planned invasion of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> indefinitely.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/september-27">27 September</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Germany, Italy and Japan sign the Tripartite Pact</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The three powers signed a ten-year military alliance in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/berlin">Berlin</a>, pledging mutual aid if attacked by a power not yet at war, aimed chiefly at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a>. It formalised the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/axis-powers">Axis</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/october-9">9 October</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">John Lennon is born in Liverpool</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">John Winston Lennon was born at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/liverpool">Liverpool</a> Maternity Hospital. As co-founder and songwriter of the Beatles, and later as a solo artist and peace campaigner, he became one of the defining figures of 20th-century popular culture.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/october-28">28 October</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Italy invades Greece from Albania</h3><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/benito-mussolini">Mussolini</a>'s forces invaded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greece">Greece</a> after Prime Minister Metaxas rejected an ultimatum. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greeks">Greeks</a> drove the Italians back into Albania, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a> invaded the following spring to rescue its ally.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greece">Greece</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/november-7">7 November</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">The Tacoma Narrows Bridge collapses</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Four months after opening, the suspension bridge over Puget Sound twisted violently in a 40-mile-per-hour wind and fell into the water. Filmed footage of 'Galloping Gertie' transformed bridge aerodynamics.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/november-14">14 November</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">The Luftwaffe devastates Coventry</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Some 500 German bombers attacked Coventry overnight, killing about 570 people and destroying the medieval cathedral. It was one of the heaviest raids of the Blitz.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/december-9">9 December</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">British forces launch Operation Compass in Egypt</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">British and Commonwealth troops attacked Italian camps in western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a>. In two months they advanced 500 miles and took some 130,000 prisoners, before Rommel's arrival turned the tide.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/london" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/london.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/december-29">29 December</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Firebombs start the 'Second Great Fire of London'</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">German bombers dropped thousands of incendiaries on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">City of London</a>, starting some 1,500 fires. Much of the square mile burned, but St Paul's Cathedral survived amid the smoke.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Campaign</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-france">Battle of France</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Battle of France was the German invasion of France and the Low Countries in May and June 1940.</p></div></li></ol></section>
